    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/jumperbridgesmod",
     "address": "key-entities/jumperbridgesmod",
     "heading": "JumperBridgesMod",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 3,
     "title": "JumperBridgesMod",
     "description": "The `UserMod2` entry point. Loads `Options` before `base.OnLoad` (which applies the patches) and sets each `BridgeKind.Enabled`, so a kind that is off has its patches skipped through `Prepare()`. Then initializes PLib, registers `ModStrings` with `Isochronous.Translations` and registers the options screen.",
     "tags": [
      "mod-entry-point",
      "mod-options",
      "mod-strings"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/options",
     "address": "key-entities/options",
     "heading": "Options",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 4,
     "title": "Options",
     "description": "PLib options saved in the shared config location, both restart-required.",
     "tags": [
      "mod-options",
      "mod-strings"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/bridgekind",
     "address": "key-entities/bridgekind",
     "heading": "BridgeKind",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 5,
     "title": "BridgeKind",
     "description": "What differs between automation and power: the network manager, layers and wire art. Two instances, `Logic` and `Power`, in `BridgeKind.All`. Each keeps its own live node table, so an automation and a power bridge end on one cell are on two separate networks. `Of(BuildingDef)` maps `BuildLocationRule.LogicBridge` to Logic and `BuildLocationRule.WireBridge` to Power; the heavy-watt joint plates have their own rule and are left alone.",
     "tags": [
      "utility-network"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/jumperbridge",
     "address": "key-entities/jumperbridge",
     "heading": "JumperBridge",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 6,
     "title": "JumperBridge",
     "description": "`KMonoBehaviour` on every complete bridge of an enabled kind. Gives each end that has no wire under it a `BridgeEndNode` (creation deferred a frame so a loaded save's wires have marked their cells first), removes the nodes when the bridge is deconstructed or broken (`BuildingBroken`) and recreates them on repair (`BuildingFullyRepaired`).",
     "tags": [
      "game-component"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/bridgeendnode",
     "address": "key-entities/bridgeendnode",
     "heading": "BridgeEndNode",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 7,
     "title": "BridgeEndNode",
     "description": "A `KAnimGraphTileVisualizer` on a standalone GameObject (no building) that stands in for a wire under a bridge end. It makes the three registrations a wire makes: the wire tile layer, a physical network node with connection bits and a network item at the cell, so the port there is told it is connected. It plays the wire kanim and mirrors the connection bits its neighbours point at it. Several bridge ends on one cell share one node, which goes with its last owner. It costs nothing, yields nothing, has no deconstruct order and is not saved. On a power network it is not a `Wire`, so the circuit's wattage limit is the bridge's own.",
     "tags": [
      "game-component",
      "utility-network"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/bridgefootprint",
     "address": "key-entities/bridgefootprint",
     "heading": "BridgeFootprint",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 8,
     "title": "BridgeFootprint",
     "description": "Registry of where every bridge is, by cell, on the complete and the under-construction prefab. The game puts a bridge on its end layer only at its two end cells and this mod stops a bridge taking that slot from a port or earlier bridge, so a bridge with both ends taken is on no layer. The deconstruct, cancel and prioritize tools find it here by its end cells.",
     "tags": [
      "game-component",
      "wire-tools"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/bridgelinks",
     "address": "key-entities/bridgelinks",
     "heading": "BridgeLinks",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 9,
     "title": "BridgeLinks",
     "description": "Owns the network manager's link table for groups of bridges that share end cells. The manager keeps one link partner per cell, so after any bridge connects or disconnects, the distinct cells of its group are rewritten as a directed ring (c0 to c1 to ... to c0), sorted so the write is idempotent, then the networks are rebuilt.",
     "tags": [
      "utility-network"
     ]
    },
    {
     "node": "mods/jumper-bridges",
     "path": "domains/entities.md",
     "id": "domains/entities.md#key-entities/harmony-patches",
     "address": "key-entities/harmony-patches",
     "heading": "Harmony patches",
     "level": 3,
     "ordinal": 10,
     "title": "Harmony patches",
     "description": "The game classes and methods patched, grouped by purpose, all in `mods/jumper-bridges/src/JumperBridges/Patches.cs`. A group is skipped when its kind is off., Bridge setup (automation): `LogicWireBridgeConfig` and `LogicRibbonBridgeConfig` `DoPostConfigureComplete` and `DoPostConfigureUnderConstruction` add `JumperBridge` and `BridgeFootprint`., Bridge setup (power): `WireBridgeConfig` `DoPostConfigureComplete` and `DoPostConfigureUnderConstruction`., Placement: `BuildingDef.MarkArea`, `AreLogicPortsInValidPositions`, `IsValidWireBridgeLocation`, `IsValidHighWattBridgeLocation`, `ArePowerPortsInValidPositions`, `MarkOverlappingPorts`., Ports: `LogicPorts.CreatePhysicalPorts`, `DestroyPhysicalPorts`, `CreateVisualizers` (skipped for bridges)., Links: `LogicUtilityNetworkLink` and `WireUtilityNetworkLink` `OnConnect` and `OnDisconnect` call `BridgeLinks`., Wire art and drags: `KAnimGraphTileVisualizer.OnSpawn`, `UpdateConnections`, `OnCleanUp`; `BaseUtilityBuildTool.BuildPath`., Tools: `DisconnectTool.OnDragComplete` and `OnMouseMove`; `DeconstructTool.DeconstructCell`; `CancelTool.OnDragTool`; `PrioritizeTool.OnDragTool`., Overlays: `OverlayModes.Logic` and `OverlayModes.Power` `Update` and `Disable`.",
     "tags": [
      "harmony-patching",
      "wire-tools"
     ]
    },
    {
